{% comment %}
  Makes the accessibility tree well-formed for Splide carousels built on <ul>/<li>.

  THE PROBLEM
  Splide labels each slide role="group", or role="tabpanel" when pagination is on.
  Neither is a permitted role on <li> — ARIA in HTML allows only listitem (implicit),
  menuitem, menuitemcheckbox, menuitemradio, option, none, presentation, radio,
  separator, tab and treeitem. The result is a <ul> whose children are not listitems,
  which PageSpeed reports as "ARIA role should be appropriate for the element" and
  "Accessibility tree is not well-formed".

  WHY THIS APPROACH
  The obvious fix is to render slides as <div>. That was tried and reverted: several
  stylesheets select these slides via a bare `li` (including nested rules in
  custom-multicolumn.scss), and swapping an element selector for a class selector also
  changes specificity from (0,4,1) to (0,5,0), which flips which rule wins against
  Dawn's own selectors. It broke the homepage layout twice.

  This removes ONLY the offending attribute. The element reverts to its implicit
  listitem role, the list becomes well-formed, and nothing about the markup, the
  cascade or the layout changes.

  aria-roledescription="slide" is deliberately KEPT — it is a global attribute, valid
  on a listitem, so screen readers still announce these as slides.

  Scoped to li.splide__slide only, so <div> based Splide carousels are untouched.
{% endcomment %}

<script>
  (function () {
    function clean(root) {
      var slides = (root || document).querySelectorAll('li.splide__slide[role]');
      for (var i = 0; i < slides.length; i++) {
        var r = slides[i].getAttribute('role');
        if (r === 'group' || r === 'tabpanel') slides[i].removeAttribute('role');
      }
    }

    // Splide sets the role at mount, and again for loop clones and on refresh.
    // Watch just the role attribute so this stays cheap.
    try {
      new MutationObserver(function (records) {
        for (var i = 0; i < records.length; i++) {
          var t = records[i].target;
          if (t.tagName === 'LI' && t.classList.contains('splide__slide')) {
            var r = t.getAttribute('role');
            if (r === 'group' || r === 'tabpanel') t.removeAttribute('role');
          }
        }
      }).observe(document.documentElement, {
        subtree: true,
        attributes: true,
        attributeFilter: ['role']
      });
    } catch (e) {}

    if (document.readyState === 'loading') {
      document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () { clean(); }, { once: true });
    } else {
      clean();
    }
    window.addEventListener('load', function () { clean(); }, { once: true });
  })();
</script>
